      "output": "Sure! Given your love of stand-up and storytelling comedy, here are a few solid picks for tonight:\n\n**Top pick: \"John Mulaney: Baby J\" (2023, Netflix)** — Since \"Kid Gorgeous\" is your favorite, this is a natural next watch. It's his newest special, and it leans even harder into storytelling as he works through a wild year of his life. Great study material for how he structures long-form personal anecdotes into punchlines.\n\n**Other options:**\n- **\"Bo Burnham: Inside\" (Netflix)** — if you want something different but brilliantly crafted; lots to learn about pacing and building a piece.\n- **\"Hacks\" (Max)** — a great TV option about a stand-up comedian; funny and genuinely insightful about the comedy world.\n- **\"Nate Bargatze: Hello World\" (2023, Prime Video)** — a masterclass in understated delivery, a nice contrast to Mulaney's style.\n\nIf you're in a learning mood before or after the workshop, \"Baby J\" doubles as entertainment and a case study in narrative joke construction. Enjoy your night!"
    },
